e that's worth  exploring and I'll be looking at that  more in the next video so this is  certainly all speculation and I maintain  that flow probably comes in a number of  different forms there's no one perfect  vision  core response to every situation even  though it'd be nice to think otherwise  but it seems that being able to stay  calm during heightened sympathetic  response is one of the keys to  performing optimally want to increase  arousal and motivation and vigilance  drink performance and dull tasks but our  aim is to control that response during  competition or intense stress we must be  a hundred percent focused to react to  reflexively and instinctively whilst  also been calm enough to prevent our  brain function from shutting down it's  the difference between being psyched out  and psyched up and in part two of this  video I'll be looking at how we can tap  into a flow state quickly and  effectively using a number of flow hacks  based on all of this theory actually  decent ones that might work including  nootropics tacks for inducing flow so  there you go I just want to shed a  little bit of light on two flow States  and how there may be a little bit more  complicated and nuanced than a lot of  people seem to think hope you found this  video useful interesting guys if you did  then please like it please share it  around it helps them greatly let me know  in the comments down below what you  think of flow state really is if you  want more information on this and links  to all the studies that I referenced and  check out the link in the description  down below and that take you to the  accompanying blog post which goes with  this video down there you'll also find  links to my social media including  Instagram and Twitter and Facebook and  on there you can follow me see what I'm  doing in the gym find out about new  posts and videos etc likewise stay tuned  and subscribe to this channel if you'd  like more videos on brain training  performance bodybuildi